     The system runs ssyynncc automatically at intervals, and as part
     of an orderly shutdown.  Running ssyynncc by hand before halting
     the processor abnormally (for example, before turning off
     power) reduces the chance of losing data, but since ssyynncc
     does not wait for the writes to complete, running it twice,
     with a short pause between, is safer still.
